  "worked_solution": "First, we find the smallest and largest $y$-values in the graph.\n\n- The smallest $y$-value is $1.$ This occurs when $x=0.$\n\n- There is no largest $y$-value.\n\nThe function covers all the $y$-values between $1$ and $\\infty ,$ including $1.$\n\nTherefore, the range is $1\\le y<\\infty ,$ which can also be written as \n$1\\le f(x)<\\infty .$",
